course: dictionary
lesson: 11891
title: Brisk and its many meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: The word brisk has more than one meaning, so use the words around it to find the right one. Look at what is being described: a walk, the wind, a person's manner, or a market.
explain: «We went for a brisk walk before breakfast.» A brisk walk is quick and full of energy, so brisk means fast and lively here. «The brisk wind made my cheeks sting.» Here brisk means cold and fresh.
explain: «The shopkeeper gave a brisk nod and went back to her counter.» This brisk means quick and businesslike, perhaps a little short. Always swap your meaning into the sentence to check that it fits.
fact: Brisk is an adjective: brisk, brisker, briskest.
fact: «Brisk» can mean quick and energetic, as in «a brisk walk».
fact: «Brisk» can describe cold, fresh weather, as in «a brisk morning».
fact: «Brisk» can describe a manner that is quick and businesslike, sometimes a little short.
fact: «Brisk» can also mean busy, as in «brisk trade» at a market, with lots of buying and selling.
exercise: «We took a brisk walk around the park.» What does brisk mean here? | *Quick and full of energy | Very loud | Cold and wet | Slow and tired
exercise: «A brisk breeze blew across the lake.» What kind of weather does this suggest? | Dark and stormy | *Cold and fresh | Hot and sticky | Foggy and still
exercise: «Business was brisk at the market all morning.» What does brisk mean? | *Busy, with lots of buying and selling | Empty and quiet | Sad and grey | Very slow
test: «The coach gave a brisk reply and turned back to the team.» What does brisk suggest about the reply? | Whispered very softly | Funny and silly | Long and friendly | *Quick and businesslike, a little short
test: Ella says brisk means slow and calm. Why is she wrong? | Brisk means very old | Brisk means the same as sad | *Brisk means quick, lively or busy | Brisk means slow, calm and sleepy
exam: Which sentence uses brisk to mean busy? | We went for a brisk walk to school | She gave a brisk wave and left the room | *Trade at the market was brisk all morning | The brisk puppy ran straight to the gate
